{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeProductSurjective"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.notMem_rad_incl_of_notMem_rad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.notMem_rad_incl_of_notMem_rad","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset.lean#L193-L207","doc":"**The tower inclusion is injective on the quotients** — `TL_m ↪ TL_{m+1}`, in the\nform \"distinct classes stay distinct\", unconditionally.\n\nContrapositive packaging of `mem_rad_of_incl_mem_rad`: an element outside the radical at\nlevel `m` stays outside it after inclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.mem_rad_of_incl_mem_rad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.mem_rad_of_incl_mem_rad","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset.lean#L175-L191","doc":"**Reflection along the tower inclusion, unconditionally.**\n\nIf `heckeIncl a` is invisible to `wtrace` at level `m+1`, then `a` is invisible at level\n`m`.  Test elements are restricted to the image: `wtrace (heckeIncl a * heckeIncl b) =\nwtrace (heckeIncl (a * b)) = wtrace (a * b)`.\n\nNo conditional expectation, and no instance of any open class — only the genericity\n`wtrace` already carries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.mem_rad_iff_twoRow_blocks_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.mem_rad_iff_twoRow_blocks_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset.lean#L138-L152","doc":"**The radical of `wtrace` is EXACTLY the three-row part.**\n\nThe two halves together: `x` is invisible to the Ocneanu trace form precisely when every\nat-most-two-row block kills it.  Equivalently, the radical is the span of the blocks with\n`ℓ(λ) ≥ 3` — which at convention D is the Temperley–Lieb ideal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.notMem_rad_of_twoRow_block_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.notMem_rad_of_twoRow_block_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset.lean#L88-L136","doc":"**⊆ : a live at-most-two-row block is visible to `wtrace`.**\n\nContrapositive of \"the radical is contained in the `ℓ(λ) ≥ 3` part\".  If some shape\nwith at most two rows does not kill `x`, then `x` is not in the radical. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.exists_trace_mul_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.exists_trace_mul_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset.lean#L60-L86","doc":"**A nonzero matrix is seen by the trace form.**\n\nPick `i j` with `M i j ≠ 0` and pair with the single-entry matrix at `(j, i)`: the\nproduct's diagonal is supported at `i`, where it reads `M i j`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}